## PROMPT 2 — WRITE A COMPLETE BUG REPORT

```
I need help writing a professional vulnerability report for a 
bug bounty competition on BOSS OS (Debian-based government Linux OS).

CONFIRMED FINDING:
Title (rough idea): [YOUR FINDING TITLE]
What I found: [DESCRIBE WHAT'S WRONG]
How I verified it: [COMMANDS YOU RAN]
Exact terminal output: [PASTE OUTPUT]
Problem Statement category: [PS-01 to PS-10, or "Others"]

Please write a complete, professional bug report with these 
EXACT sections:

1. VULNERABILITY TITLE (specific, includes the component and issue)
2. BOSS OS VERSION (I'll fill in the exact version)
3. AFFECTED COMPONENT (specific file/service/config)
4. VULNERABILITY DESCRIPTION (2-4 sentences, clear and technical)
5. STEPS TO REPRODUCE (numbered, anyone can follow)
6. PROOF OF CONCEPT (exact commands + exact output format)
7. IMPACT ASSESSMENT (what can an attacker actually do - be specific 
   about government/sensitive data risk)
8. PROPOSED SEVERITY + JUSTIFICATION (Critical/High/Medium/Low 
   with CVSS 3.1 score and vector string)
9. SUGGESTED REMEDIATION (exact commands to fix it)
10. RELEVANT CWE NUMBER (if applicable)

Make the impact section specific to a GOVERNMENT operating system 
handling sensitive citizen/administrative data — not generic.
Keep technical accuracy high. Do not exaggerate severity beyond 
what the evidence supports.
```

