## PROMPT 3 — CHAIN MULTIPLE BUGS TOGETHER

```
I found multiple individual security issues on a Linux system 
(BOSS OS bug bounty competition) and I think they might combine 
into a more severe attack chain. Help me figure out if they 
genuinely chain together, and if so, write a combined report.

MY INDIVIDUAL FINDINGS:

Finding 1: [TITLE] - [SEVERITY] - [BRIEF DESCRIPTION]
Evidence: [COMMAND OUTPUT]

Finding 2: [TITLE] - [SEVERITY] - [BRIEF DESCRIPTION]  
Evidence: [COMMAND OUTPUT]

Finding 3: [TITLE] - [SEVERITY] - [BRIEF DESCRIPTION]
Evidence: [COMMAND OUTPUT]

(add more findings if you have them)

Please:
1. Tell me HONESTLY if these findings actually chain together into 
   a real attack path, or if they are unrelated (don't force a 
   connection that doesn't make sense)
2. If they DO chain, walk me through the exact attack sequence 
   step by step
3. What additional verification should I do to PROVE the chain works 
   end-to-end (not just theoretically)?
4. Write a combined vulnerability report following this structure:
   - Title (describing the full chain)
   - Individual vulnerabilities in the chain
   - Steps to reproduce the FULL chain
   - Proof of concept for each step
   - Combined impact assessment
   - Overall severity with justification
   - Remediation for the whole chain

Be skeptical - if the chain doesn't genuinely hold together, 
tell me to submit them separately instead.
```

